cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SuperBLAST (BLAST Hub): bulk sequence search on managed NCBI BLAST+ infrastructure"
message: "If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  # Mononym: recorded with given-names only. CFF 1.2.0 allows a person with a
  # single name; adding a family-names field would invent a surname.
  - given-names: Vipin
    email: sainivipin839@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2924-7095"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vipin839/superblast"
url: "https://superblast.app"
abstract: >-
  SuperBLAST is a web application for bulk sequence similarity searching. It
  executes genuine NCBI BLAST+ searches - blastn, blastp, blastx, tblastn and
  tblastx - against pre-indexed reference databases on managed cloud
  infrastructure, and returns native JSON-15 output parsed into an interactive
  hit table with per-HSP pairwise alignments. Nucleotide and protein databases
  are provided for each reference organism, pinned to specific NCBI assembly
  accessions with recorded SHA-256 checksums and taxonomy identifiers; the build
  verifies every database with blastdbcmd and runs one search per program before
  the image ships. A submission takes up to 100 FASTA files, and results export
  as a multi-sheet Excel workbook, a PDF report, or raw JSON and CSV.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - BLAST
  - sequence alignment
  - nucleotide
  - protein
  - genomics
  - sequence data management
  - research software
  - web application
license: MIT
version: 2.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-10"

